I just realized that one of my favorite character 
classes isn't represented -- The Berserker.

Here's a possible implementation:

Berserker
Alignment: Chaotic

Stats: Similar to Barbarian
Intrinsics:
Level 1:
Ability to go Berserk. (#berserk command)
The following occurs when berserk:
- All damage incurred by the character is multiplied by 
1/2 (rounded up)
- Character becomes Poison Resistant, Sleep Resistant 
and gains Speed.
- Damage done by the character is multipled by 1.5 
(Rounding down)
- Character Aggravates monsters as per the ring.
- Character can not distinguish between peaceful, tame 
and hostile monsters.
- The character becomes partially uncontrolled.  Each 
turn, the character has a 75% to automatically charge 
toward the nearest monster if none are next to him, and 
a 90% chance to attack a monster that is next to him.  
Otherwise, the character may move and act normally.

Going Berserk takes one turn, and costs no energy.  The 
character will remain berserk as long as monsters are 
visable.  The character may only go berserk if hostile 
monsters are visable.

Let me know what you think.

